      - Definitions: {"Movies_and_TV:gru_padding_audit": "Fixed training-independent item-ID fixtures cover empty, singleton, short, full loader-width, tied-length and mixed-length histories. A CPU float64 reference applies PyTorch reset/update/new GRU gate equations, including reset-after-recurrent-affine candidate bias, and preserves every layer state at padding. Every independent history starts from zero. The reference must first match native individually unpadded CPU float64 GRU outputs at atol=rtol=1e-7. Then eval-mode ModelView outputs, final features, raw candidate scores, isolated histories, batch permutations, added leading padding, repeated calls and calls after unrelated histories are checked with autocast disabled at atol=1e-5, rtol=1.3e-6. Failing elements violate abs(actual-reference)<=atol+rtol*abs(reference), including nonfinite elements. Relative L2 uses a 1e-30 denominator floor. Backend escalation disables TF32, then cuDNN only after failure, preserving thresholds and restoring original settings. Persistent failure additionally checks the actual encoder on CPU float64 at atol=rtol=1e-7, using identical recurrent parameters and a copied embedding prefix containing every fixture/candidate ID. This temporary diagnostic copy is never fitted or deployed. CPU checks cover aligned features, final features, scores and added padding; other execution checks remain in the preceding backend stages. The minimum rank-10/11 reference gap excludes empty histories, whose all-zero scores otherwise force that minimum to zero. Candidate IDs 1..min(itemnum,100) are fixed audit candidates, not validation labels; rank changes refer to candidate 1. Stable sorting breaks ties by candidate order. Top-10 overlap and the minimum reference rank-10/11 score gap describe numerical rank sensitivity. An unverified reference leaves execution checks unavailable. The supplied encoder already compacts and packs real tokens, so this audit leaves its architecture, loss, sampler, optimizer, checkpoint selection and matching imported predictor unchanged. Failures do not automatically establish a semantic defect; no validation improvement, gradient equivalence or predictor-export equivalence is established by these diagnostic measurements.", "Movies_and_TV:context_sensitivity": "At most 64 eligible rows from the first two cached training batches. Each row has at least three real inputs and distinct nonzero latest positive/negative targets. Remove k events from either prefix or suffix, with k uniform in 1..n-2 using a dedicated seed-42 RNG. Both interventions retain the original latest target and identical two-item candidate pool. Margin deltas are perturbed minus full-context positive-negative margins; rank deltas are changes in zero-based positive rank among those two items (positive wins ties), so positive rank deltas mean deterioration. Feature cosines measure sensitivity, not usefulness. Length and removed means describe sampled input and removal event counts; length strata use original input lengths. Suffix removal also increases the event gap to the fixed target, so it is not a pure forgetting control. Padding error is the maximum absolute final-feature difference for identical chronological real inputs under different padding: compare original padded rows against compacted real inputs; for full-length rows, compare against one added leading zero. Measurements use eval mode. padding_check_passed reports whether the maximum error is at most the declared absolute tolerance of 1e-5; this is a numerical diagnostic, not a proof of recurrence correctness. Failure confounds context deltas with padding-induced state changes. Null denotes no eligible measurements. Timestamp gap strata are unavailable because loader batches do not include timestamps. These are conditional training diagnostics, not HR@10, unseen full-catalog ranks, or evidence that cropped training improves validation. No model scores are fused.", "Movies_and_TV:embedding_collapse_score"